# ============================================================================
#  sumi-files.list — what Sumi-Files manages, relative to ~/.config
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Read by three tools, so they can never disagree:
#    install.sh       repo → ~/.config   (config/<entry> → ~/.config/<entry>)
#    bin/dotbackup    ~/.config → repo   (and `dotbackup --check`)
#    hypr/scripts/dotbackup-remind.sh   (through `dotbackup --check`)
#
#  Syntax (docs/DOTBACKUP.md § Manifest):
#    dir/            a whole directory, mirrored (files deleted at the source
#                    are deleted in the repo)
#    file            a single file
#    src => dst      different name in the repo (dst is relative to config/)
#    ~/path          a source outside ~/.config, relative to $HOME
#  Absolute paths and '..' are rejected.
#
#  systemd/, gtk-*/ and qt*ct/ are listed file by file on purpose: those
#  folders also hold machine state (enabled-unit symlinks, GTK bookmarks with
#  recent paths, qt*ct window geometry) and units you may not want public.
#  A versioned file in one of those folders that leaves this list is deleted
#  from the repo on the next dotbackup.
# ============================================================================

cava/
fastfetch/
fish/
hypr/
hyprlock/
kitty/
matugen/
sumi-shell/

starship.static.toml

systemd/user/hyprland-session.service
